WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.770
We're still a few months out from the release
of Joker, the film from director Todd Phillips

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.280
in which Joaquin Phoenix takes on the role
of Batman's arch-enemy.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.410
But it's already sparking controversy among
DC fans with a possible plot twist that would

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:17.040
add a whole lot more than just a name to the
Joker's origin story.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:23.120
Citing a "source close to the production,"
We Got This Covered reported on May 27th that

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.730
Joker might be set to include a contentious
curveball: the Clown Prince of Crime and his

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.720
superhero nemesis Batman are actually related.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:35.100
The film will apparently establish this personal
connection by revealing that Arthur Fleck

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.190
— the real name given to the Joker in the
upcoming movie — is actually the product

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:44.100
of an affair that Bruce Wayne's father Thomas,
played by Brett Cullen, had with Arthur's

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:44.600
mother.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.260
"She told me I had a purpose.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:51.800
To bring laughter and joy to the world."

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:56.800
For those of you keeping score at home, that
would mean that the Joker is Batman's half-brother.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.840
This isn't the first time this rumor has cropped
up.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.580
We saw it last year, along with other hearsay
that has since proven to be true, including

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:08.100
Robert De Niro being cast as the talk show
host Murray Franklin.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:12.720
If that's the case here, it seems like a pretty
logical way for Joker to connect itself to

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.260
some version of the larger Batman mythology.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:20.600
We've known for a while that Cullen's Thomas
Wayne was going to be depicted as a more antagonistic

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:25.850
character than most moviegoers might expect
considering previous incarnations of Batman's

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:29.120
dad, and the plot twist even makes sense from
a casting standpoint.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:34.360
The part of young Bruce Wayne will be played
in the film by Dante Pereira-Olson, a child

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:39.021
actor who previously played the younger version
of Phoenix's character in 2017's You Were

00:01:39.021 --> 00:01:40.200
Never Really Here.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.880
Hey, if one casting team thought they looked
alike, the Joker gang might have, too.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.800
Though the Joker has never been revealed as
the half-sibling of Bruce Wayne in the comics,

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.120
the Dark Knight has been previously portrayed
as having a villainous brother.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:59.070
Back in 1974, Thomas Wayne Jr. was introduced
in the pages of World's Finest #223 as the

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.380
older brother Batman never knew he had.

00:02:01.829 --> 00:02:06.480
As the comic explains, Thomas Jr. had been
hit by a car as a baby, and the resulting

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.320
brain damage led to him being raised in Willowood
Sanitarium rather than Wayne Manor.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.239
The Waynes never got around to telling their
other son about him before they were murdered

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:20.340
in Crime Alley, so Thomas Jr.'s return came
as quite a surprise to Batman, especially

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.820
since Junior was being manipulated into murdering
people with razor-sharp boomerangs.

00:02:25.129 --> 00:02:29.520
He then got his body taken over by the ghostly
superhero Deadman, who used it to get a job

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.549
at the circus.

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:34.900
A modern version of Thomas also exists, and
while he keeps the name and some of the basics

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:38.680
of the origin story, the direction of the
character was very different.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:43.819
He used the name "Lincoln March" to run for
mayor and operated as an assassin for a secretive

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:44.969
Gotham City cult.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.580
He told Batman that he was actually Thomas
Wayne Jr., born prematurely as a result of

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:53.560
a car accident, and proved that Martha Wayne
had come to visit him when he was growing

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.020
up at the Willowood Orphanage.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.920
A DNA test, however, proved to be inconclusive.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:03.540
The "Thomas Wayne Jr." name was also used
for Owlman, Batman's counterpart on an alternate

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.740
Earth where the heroes are all villains.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:09.660
However, none of those characters have ever
operated as the Joker.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:14.290
In fact, in the comics, the Joker has never
been given an official "real name" or origin

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:19.130
story for who he was before he took a dip
in a vat of acid and emerged as one of Gotham's

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.380
greatest terrors.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:25.300
Even The Killing Joke was intended as only
a possible origin rather than a definitive

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:29.480
one, and there have been several intentionally
conflicting origins published since.

00:03:29.769 --> 00:03:33.780
So if the rumored "Batman and the Joker are
brothers" plot twist in Joker turns out to

00:03:33.791 --> 00:03:37.989
be true, it would definitely give viewers
something they hadn't seen before.

00:03:37.989 --> 00:03:40.100
Catch Joker in theaters on October 4th.

